{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.AntipodeDetermined","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.AntipodeDetermined","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Conv","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Hopf_"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.antipode_sq_of_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.antipode_sq_of_comm","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/AntipodeDetermined.lean#L192-L213","doc":"**`S² = id` needs commutativity — it does not follow from the Hopf axioms\nalone.**\n\nA re-export of `HopfObj.antipode_antipode`, so that the\nhypothesis `comm` is visible from inside this corpus.  `comm` says the\nmultiplication is invariant under the braiding; for a genuinely\n`q`-deformed substrate it is exactly what fails, which is why `S² = id`\nshould not be expected here.\n\nStated for Mathlib's `HopfObj` rather than for `FrobeniusHopfData`,\nbecause the latter carries no bimonoid compatibility (see the module\ndocstring) and so is not a Hopf monoid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_eq_of_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_eq_of_left","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/AntipodeDetermined.lean#L180-L185","doc":"Restated with the sides swapped, for rewriting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_unique","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/AntipodeDetermined.lean#L167-L178","doc":"**Uniqueness of the antipode**, in the usual two-sided form: anything\nsatisfying both antipode axioms is the antipode.\n\nWeaker than `antipode_unique_of_left`, which needs only the left one —\nrecorded in that direction because a theorem should not carry a hypothesis\nit does not spend. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_unique_of_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode_unique_of_left","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/AntipodeDetermined.lean#L139-L165","doc":"**Uniqueness of the antipode.**  Any morphism satisfying the two antipode\naxioms *is* the antipode.\n\nThis is what the 2026-09-14 axiom addition buys: `antipode` stops being\nfree data.  Before it, `S` could be replaced by any endomorphism whatever\nand every law still held (`AntipodeIndependence.withAntipode`); now it is\npinned by `(μ, η, Δ, ε)`.\n\nProof: `S'` is a left convolution inverse of `𝟙` and `F.antipode` is a\nright one, and in a monoid left and right inverses coincide.  The monoid\nis `CategoryTheory.Conv F.obj F.obj`, whose `Monoid` instance is exactly\nwhere the associativity, coassociativity and unit/counit laws are spent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.toComonObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.toComonObj","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/AntipodeDetermined.lean#L129-L135","doc":"The coalgebra half of a `FrobeniusHopfData` is a Mathlib `ComonObj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.toMonObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.toMonObj","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/AntipodeDetermined.lean#L119-L127","doc":"The algebra half of a `FrobeniusHopfData` is a Mathlib `MonObj`.\nField-for-field: the six laws were given Mathlib's exact shapes so that\nthis is a transport rather than a proof. ","signatureChunk":0}]}